  "question": {
    "text": "A system of three polarizers <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is set up such that the pass axis of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> is crossed with respect to that of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> . The pass axis of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> is inclined at <math><msup><mrow><mn>60</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math> to the pass axis of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math> When a beam of unpolarized light of intensity <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></math> is incident on <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> the intensity of light transmitted by the three polarizers is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> . The ratio <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> equals (nearly):",
    "image": null
  },
